#
# Gaming patches of the nazoos kernel flavor, in apply order.
# Format: <file name in patches/> <URL | local>
# Pinned to commits/paths for one kernel series (KERNEL_SERIES in
# make-obs-package.sh). On a new kernel series: update the URLs (CachyOS
# keeps one directory / branch per series), run fetch-patches.sh and
# make-obs-package.sh --check.
#
# Sources:
#   https://github.com/CachyOS/kernel-patches   (patch files per series)
#   https://github.com/CachyOS/linux             (branches <series>/<topic>)

# BORE scheduler (Burst-Oriented Response Enhancer) without the CachyOS
# base patch. "local": kernel-patches/7.3 only has the bore-cachy variant;
# its fair.c hunk that removes CachyOS' CONFIG_CACHY base_slice/
# migration_cost blocks is rewritten to vanilla context, the rest is
# unchanged. Upstream:
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CachyOS/kernel-patches/master/7.3/sched/0001-bore-cachy.patch
0001-bore.patch                    local
# BBRv3 TCP congestion control (branch 7.3/bbr3)
0002-tcp-bbr3.patch                https://github.com/CachyOS/linux/commit/5b121d2f9e4f.patch
0003-tcp-bbr3-name.patch           https://github.com/CachyOS/linux/commit/a52f724cc56d.patch
# ACS override (pcie_acs_override=), for PCI passthrough to VMs (branch 7.3/cachy)
0004-pci-acs-override.patch        https://github.com/CachyOS/linux/commit/16acc33ed004.patch
# v4l2loopback 0.15.4 in-tree, as module (branch 7.3/cachy)
0005-v4l2loopback.patch            https://github.com/CachyOS/linux/commit/930f739a0202.patch
# Handheld support: panel orientation, MSI Claw, Zotac Zone, Ayaneo/GPD/
# OneXPlayer audio and fan quirks, Steam Deck backlight (branch 7.3/handheld).
# "local": the drivers/hid/Makefile zotac-zone-hid hunk is anchored after
# amd-sfh-hid (CachyOS' tree has Apple spi-hid/dockchannel lines there that
# SUSE's tree does not have), the rest is unchanged. Upstream:
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CachyOS/kernel-patches/master/7.3/misc/0001-handheld.patch
0007-handheld.patch                local
# tsc=directsync: CPUs without IA32_TSC_ADJUST (Steam Deck, Zen 2 APUs)
# sync their TSCs by writing the TSC directly and restore it after sleep,
# so the TSC stays a stable clocksource after resume. Only active with the
# boot option tsc=directsync (nazoos-welcome, Gaming page). From Valve's
# Steam Deck kernel, carried in branch 7.3/cachy (the 7.2 fixup for the
# rdmsrq/wrmsrq rename is folded into the first commit)
0008-tsc-directsync.patch          https://github.com/CachyOS/linux/commit/d77c58de7881.patch
0009-tsc-watchdog.patch            https://github.com/CachyOS/linux/commit/dd199fccf526.patch
0010-tsc-save-restore.patch        https://github.com/CachyOS/linux/commit/63239e08d7ef.patch
0011-tsc-restore-only.patch        https://github.com/CachyOS/linux/commit/9d04311179f0.patch
0012-tsc-no-random-warps.patch     https://github.com/CachyOS/linux/commit/e5c2a5fd8c3a.patch
0013-tsc-revert-extra-time.patch   https://github.com/CachyOS/linux/commit/f9012d5b1220.patch
# 0015-0020 (dmem cgroup VRAM protection, ADR 0013) dropped: the series
# is upstream in Linux 7.3; dmemcg-booster uses it as before.
# HDMI 2.1 VRR (HDMI Forum VRR: TVs and monitors without FreeSync, more
# DP-to-HDMI adapters) and ALLM for amdgpu. Branch 7.3/hdmi (Tomasz
# Pakuła) as one diff from its base (Linux 7.3-rc4) to the branch head
0021-amdgpu-hdmi-vrr.patch         https://github.com/CachyOS/linux/compare/93f51579e7df...96f023bb8c13.diff
# Nobara 7.2 patches (Nobara-Project/rpm-sources, pinned to commit
# 93742e4b, dir baseos/kernel/mainline/7.2), not in 7.3 or Kernel:stable;
# Nobara has no 7.3 directory yet, they apply to 7.3 unchanged.
# Poll rate per USB device: usbcore.interrupt_interval_override=VID:PID:ms
# (e.g. wired PS4/PS5 controllers at 1000 Hz). "local": context of the
# kernel-parameters.txt hunk adapted (new usbcore quirk flag in 7.2);
# parser fix: len as int for %n (size_t len oopsed on every write, see
# patch header).
# Upstream: https://github.com/KarsMulder/Linux-Pollrate-Patch, via
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nobara-Project/rpm-sources/93742e4be6d092388742a0f5b60b37d719b719e7/baseos/kernel/mainline/7.2/0001-Allow-to-set-custom-USB-pollrate-for-specific-device.patch
0022-usb-pollrate-override.patch   local
# Hardware quirks: ROG Ally sensors (nct6775 board RC71L), Logitech G923
# PlayStation version, ASUS laptop keyboards (usbhid), RDNA1/RDNA2 dGPU
# suspend (amdgpu gfx10 CSIB), ASUS I226-V rev 6 on one board (1043:8867)
# drops off the bus (igc, ASPM L1)
# 0023 "local": context refreshed for 7.2.9. Upstream:
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nobara-Project/rpm-sources/93742e4be6d092388742a0f5b60b37d719b719e7/baseos/kernel/mainline/7.2/ROG-ALLY-NCT6775-PLATFORM.patch
0023-nct6775-rog-ally.patch        local
0024-hid-logitech-g923-ps.patch    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nobara-Project/rpm-sources/93742e4be6d092388742a0f5b60b37d719b719e7/baseos/kernel/mainline/7.2/ps-logitech-wheel.patch
# 0025-btusb-qca9377 dropped: in Linux 7.2.10 ("Bluetooth: btusb: Add IMC
# Networks QCA9377 to quirks table", same ID 0x13d3:0x3503)
0026-usbhid-skip-polling.patch     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nobara-Project/rpm-sources/93742e4be6d092388742a0f5b60b37d719b719e7/baseos/kernel/mainline/7.2/0001-skip-interrupt-in-polling-for-devices.patch
0027-amdgpu-gfx10-csib.patch       https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nobara-Project/rpm-sources/93742e4be6d092388742a0f5b60b37d719b719e7/baseos/kernel/mainline/7.2/drm-amdgpu-restore-csib-submission-on-gfx10-dgpus.patch
0028-igc-i226v-aspm.patch          https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nobara-Project/rpm-sources/93742e4be6d092388742a0f5b60b37d719b719e7/baseos/kernel/mainline/7.2/igc-disable-aspm-l1-asus-i226-v.patch
# Sound on Samsung Galaxy Book 4/5 laptops, whose speakers sit behind a
# MAX98390 amplifier that 7.3 does not drive yet. Branch 7.3/snd-codecs
# (on 7.3-rc1) as one diff; new options in config/nazoos.fragment.
# Lenovo Legion Pro (AW88399) and Razer Blade 16 2025 of the 7.2 branch
# are upstream in 7.3.
0029-snd-codecs.patch              https://github.com/CachyOS/linux/compare/cee9395acd80...eec9fb473ef7.diff
